  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public Information Campaign to Deter Potential Irregular Maritime Migration from Vietnam to Australia in 2022-23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the success of previous campaign phases, the campaign will be focused on deterring irregular migration from the key source and transit provinces in Viet Nam, by effectively informing the target population about safe and lawful migration, while also delivering messages containing Australia&#x2019;s strong border protection policies, the criminal nature of people smuggling and the risks of engaging their services, and the consequences of irregular maritime migration to Australia. In this new phase, the campaign will also introduce a social media outreach component which is expected to effectively grasp the attention of the younger populations, who comprise the majority of aspirant (regular and irregular) migrants. In addition, IOM will conduct quarterly analysis of migration trends and sentiments among populations in the target hotspot provinces. These data and analysis will offer up-to-date picture of the migration scene on the grounds and feed into future programming on counter-smuggling and prevention of irregular migration. As a result of this campaign, target populations will have enhanced understanding of the risks and dangers associated with irregular maritime migration, which contribute to positive behaviour change and prevent people from using services offered by migrant smugglers to reach Australia.</narrative>
  </description>
